{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794589482149,"sessionID":"ses_e2a222b13ffegJo45ooHszMORK","part":{"partID":"prt_1d5de56ae0023z5xCaevb3SQcW","sessionID":"ses_e2a222b13ffegJo45ooHszMORK","messageID":"msg_1d5de2ba400107cNZ9fxGolAXN","type":"tool","id":"call_5cb0410a9c0e46e3a8b1b8e9","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/017-review-pass-two-remediation/scratch/planning/probe-catalog-lines.sh"},"output":"Read file /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/017-review-pass-two-remediation/scratch/planning/probe-catalog-lines.sh, lines 1-11\n1: #!/bin/bash\n2: # Run from the repository root: bash <this file>\n3: # Prints every file:line citation on the advisor-recommend catalog page with the\n4: # line it points at today, so a stale citation shows the wrong code. Reads only.\n5: ADV=.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime\n6: HK=.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks\n7: ARM=.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog/cli-surface/advisor-recommend.md\n8: rg -o '`(schemas/advisor-tool-schemas\\.ts|handlers/advisor-recommend\\.ts|tools/advisor-recommend\\.ts|skill-advisor-cli-manifest\\.ts|hooks/lib/skill-advisor-cli-fallback\\.ts):[0-9]+' \"$ARM\" | tr -d '`' | sort -u | while IFS=: read -r file line; do\n9:   base=$ADV; [ \"${file#hooks/}\" != \"$file\" ] && base=$HK && file=${file#hooks/}\n10:   printf '%s:%s => %s\\n' \"$file\" \"$line\" \"$(sed -n \"${line}p\" \"$base/$file\" | sed 's/^ *//' | cut -c1-70)\"\n11: done","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/017-review-pass-two-remediation/scratch/planning/probe-catalog-lines.sh, lines 1-11\n1: #!/bin/bash\n2: # Run from the repository root: bash <this file>\n3: # Prints every file:line citation on the advisor-recommend catalog page with the\n4: # line it points at today, so a stale citation shows the wrong code. Reads only.\n5: ADV=.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime\n6: HK=.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks\n7: ARM=.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog/cli-surface/advisor-recommend.md\n8: rg -o '`(schemas/advisor-tool-schemas\\.ts|handlers/advisor-recommend\\.ts|tools/advisor-recommend\\.ts|skill-advisor-cli-manifest\\.ts|hooks/lib/skill-advisor-cli-fallback\\.ts):[0-9]+' \"$ARM\" | tr -d '`' | sort -u | while IFS=: read -r file line; do\n9:   base=$ADV; [ \"${file#hooks/}\" != \"$file\" ] && base=$HK && file=${file#hooks/}\n10:   printf '%s:%s => %s\\n' \"$file\" \"$line\" \"$(sed -n \"${line}p\" \"$base/$file\" | sed 's/^ *//' | cut -c1-70)\"\n11: done"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\":\"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/017-review-pass-two-remediation/scratch/planning/probe-catalog-lines.sh\"}"},"time":{"start":1794589480622,"end":1794589482149}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794589482205,"sessionID":"ses_e2a222b13ffegJo45ooHszMORK","part":{"partID":"prt_1d5de5938001k2rC118GHBBKeV","sessionID":"ses_e2a222b13ffegJo45ooHszMORK","messageID":"msg_1d5de2ba400107cNZ9fxGolAXN","type":"tool","id":"call_1d620b8b5c1c4c4a880b4acd","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"rg -n \"advisor-tool-schemas\\.ts:[0-9]|handlers/advisor-recommend\\.ts:[0-9]\" .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog/cli-surface/advisor-recommend.md","workdir":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research"},"output":"31:Each recommendation carries an optional `compiledRoute` field (`schemas/advisor-tool-schemas.ts:308`, `z.record(z.string(), z.unknown()).optional()`). `handlers/advisor-recommend.ts`'s `enrichCompiledRoutes()` attaches it only when at least one recommended `skillId` is both in the fixed 7-hub `COMPILED_ROUTING_HUBS` set and currently permitted by the tri-state `SPECKIT_COMPILED_ROUTING` flag (`compiledRoutingEnabledForHub()`, from `../lib/compiled-routing-flag.ts`). Otherwise the schema re-parse is skipped entirely and the output returns unchanged. When enrichment runs, `compiledRouteForRecommendation()` shells out to `.skilled/bin/compiled-route.cjs --hub <skillId> --prompt-stdin`, writes the prompt to its stdin and attaches the parsed result. The one exception is a result whose `servingAuthority` is `\"legacy\"`: the field then stays absent, because a legacy sentinel is never surfaced as if it were a compiled decision. A subprocess failure is handled the same way: silently no `compiledRoute` field, with an optional debug-gated stderr breadcrumb via `SPECKIT_COMPILED_ROUTING_DEBUG`, so a probe failure degrades to exactly what an ineligible or flag-off recommendation already looks like. In short, `compiledRoute` is attached only for an eligible, flag-permitted hub that is genuinely serving compiled. It is intentionally absent for every other combination: flag off, hub not in `COMPILED_ROUTING_HUBS`, legacy sentinel or probe failure. See [`feature-flag-governance.md`](../../../system-spec-kit/feature-catalog/governance/feature-flag-governance.md) for the flag's phased-default and serving-status contract, and each eligible hub's own `compiled-routing-and-legacy-fallback.md` catalog leaf for the hub-side directive this enrichment mirrors. The front door runs from the request's `workspaceRoot`, and a caller may name another checkout there, such as a worktree under the repository root. So the handler first checks that the front door it would run reads `--prompt-stdin`. An older front door gets no call and the recommendation carries no `compiledRoute`, because it would route an empty prompt.\n33:When a recommendation gets a `compiledRoute`, `enrichCompiledRoutes()` also asks `attachCommand()` in `lib/command-attach.ts` for a slash command and sets the optional `command` field when one comes back (`schemas/advisor-tool-schemas.ts:310`, `z.string().min(1).optional()`). `attachCommand()` names a command only for a `route` decision with `selectionKind: 'single'` and exactly one target, and only when the generated `MODE_COMMANDS` table maps that hub and `workflowMode` to a command. A bundle, a multi-target route or a mode with no command leaves `command` off. For `system-deep-loop` the prompt must type the same command or hold a phrase from `DEPTH_WORDING`, so a prompt that only names a topic such as research or review gets no deep-loop command. A prompt that matches `NO_EDIT_REQUEST` gets no command from any hub, because a reader who rules out a change is never handed work that writes.\n35:The request option `options.includeCompiledRoute` is an optional boolean that defaults to true. When a caller passes `false` the handler skips `enrichCompiledRoutes()` on both the fresh and the cached return (`handlers/advisor-recommend.ts:563-565`, `632-634`), so no `compiled-route.cjs` subprocess starts and no recommendation carries `compiledRoute` or `command`. The prompt hooks pass `true` (`hooks/lib/skill-advisor-cli-fallback.ts:238`), because the `command` field is derived from the compiled route. The OpenCode plugin does not pass the option and keeps receiving `compiledRoute`. The option is declared in the zod schema (`schemas/advisor-tool-schemas.ts:287`), the tool descriptor (`tools/advisor-recommend.ts:23`) and the CLI manifest (`skill-advisor-cli-manifest.ts:57`).\n37:The request option `options.compiledRouteTopOnly` is an optional boolean that defaults to false. When a caller passes `true`, `enrichCompiledRoutes()` runs the route lookup for the first recommendation only and returns every later one unchanged, so only the top pick can carry `compiledRoute` or `command`. Each lookup is a `compiled-route.cjs` subprocess, so this saves one subprocess for each further eligible hub. The prompt hooks pass `true` with `includeCompiledRoute: true`, because the brief leads with the top pick. The option is declared in the zod schema (`schemas/advisor-tool-schemas.ts:290`), the tool descriptor (`tools/advisor-recommend.ts:24`) and the CLI manifest (`skill-advisor-cli-manifest.ts:58`).\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"31:Each recommendation carries an optional `compiledRoute` field (`schemas/advisor-tool-schemas.ts:308`, `z.record(z.string(), z.unknown()).optional()`). `handlers/advisor-recommend.ts`'s `enrichCompiledRoutes()` attaches it only when at least one recommended `skillId` is both in the fixed 7-hub `COMPILED_ROUTING_HUBS` set and currently permitted by the tri-state `SPECKIT_COMPILED_ROUTING` flag (`compiledRoutingEnabledForHub()`, from `../lib/compiled-routing-flag.ts`). Otherwise the schema re-parse is skipped entirely and the output returns unchanged. When enrichment runs, `compiledRouteForRecommendation()` shells out to `.skilled/bin/compiled-route.cjs --hub <skillId> --prompt-stdin`, writes the prompt to its stdin and attaches the parsed result. The one exception is a result whose `servingAuthority` is `\"legacy\"`: the field then stays absent, because a legacy sentinel is never surfaced as if it were a compiled decision. A subprocess failure is handled the same way: silently no `compiledRoute` field, with an optional debug-gated stderr breadcrumb via `SPECKIT_COMPILED_ROUTING_DEBUG`, so a probe failure degrades to exactly what an ineligible or flag-off recommendation already looks like. In short, `compiledRoute` is attached only for an eligible, flag-permitted hub that is genuinely serving compiled. It is intentionally absent for every other combination: flag off, hub not in `COMPILED_ROUTING_HUBS`, legacy sentinel or probe failure. See [`feature-flag-governance.md`](../../../system-spec-kit/feature-catalog/governance/feature-flag-governance.md) for the flag's phased-default and serving-status contract, and each eligible hub's own `compiled-routing-and-legacy-fallback.md` catalog leaf for the hub-side directive this enrichment mirrors. The front door runs from the request's `workspaceRoot`, and a caller may name another checkout there, such as a worktree under the repository root. So the handler first checks that the front door it would run reads `--prompt-stdin`. An older front door gets no call and the recommendation carries no `compiledRoute`, because it would route an empty prompt.\n33:When a recommendation gets a `compiledRoute`, `enrichCompiledRoutes()` also asks `attachCommand()` in `lib/command-attach.ts` for a slash command and sets the optional `command` field when one comes back (`schemas/advisor-tool-schemas.ts:310`, `z.string().min(1).optional()`). `attachCommand()` names a command only for a `route` decision with `selectionKind: 'single'` and exactly one target, and only when the generated `MODE_COMMANDS` table maps that hub and `workflowMode` to a command. A bundle, a multi-target route or a mode with no command leaves `command` off. For `system-deep-loop` the prompt must type the same command or hold a phrase from `DEPTH_WORDING`, so a prompt that only names a topic such as research or review gets no deep-loop command. A prompt that matches `NO_EDIT_REQUEST` gets no command from any hub, because a reader who rules out a change is never handed work that writes.\n35:The request option `options.includeCompiledRoute` is an optional boolean that defaults to true. When a caller passes `false` the handler skips `enrichCompiledRoutes()` on both the fresh and the cached return (`handlers/advisor-recommend.ts:563-565`, `632-634`), so no `compiled-route.cjs` subprocess starts and no recommendation carries `compiledRoute` or `command`. The prompt hooks pass `true` (`hooks/lib/skill-advisor-cli-fallback.ts:238`), because the `command` field is derived from the compiled route. The OpenCode plugin does not pass the option and keeps receiving `compiledRoute`. The option is declared in the zod schema (`schemas/advisor-tool-schemas.ts:287`), the tool descriptor (`tools/advisor-recommend.ts:23`) and the CLI manifest (`skill-advisor-cli-manifest.ts:57`).\n37:The request option `options.compiledRouteTopOnly` is an optional boolean that defaults to false. When a caller passes `true`, `enrichCompiledRoutes()` runs the route lookup for the first recommendation only and returns every later one unchanged, so only the top pick can carry `compiledRoute` or `command`. Each lookup is a `compiled-route.cjs` subprocess, so this saves one subprocess for each further eligible hub. The prompt hooks pass `true` with `includeCompiledRoute: true`, because the brief leads with the top pick. The option is declared in the zod schema (`schemas/advisor-tool-schemas.ts:290`), the tool descriptor (`tools/advisor-recommend.ts:24`) and the CLI manifest (`skill-advisor-cli-manifest.ts:58`).\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"rg -n \\\"advisor-tool-schemas\\\\.ts:[0-9]|handlers/advisor-recommend\\\\.ts:[0-9]\\\" .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog/cli-surface/advisor-recommend.md\",\"workdir\":\"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research\"}"},"time":{"start":1794589481272,"end":1794589482205}}}}
