{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794589598543,"sessionID":"ses_e2a222b13ffegJo45ooHszMORK","part":{"partID":"prt_1d5e01f60002LbyvTDyNkEU3jp","sessionID":"ses_e2a222b13ffegJo45ooHszMORK","messageID":"msg_1d5e010c4001zjkXSRcbeZRMcU","type":"tool","id":"call_2aeb369616944a21b2d660ee","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"git -c core.fsmonitor=false diff --stat -- .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog/cli-surface/advisor-recommend.md\ngit -c core.fsmonitor=false diff -- .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog/cli-surface/advisor-recommend.md","workdir":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research"},"output":" .../feature-catalog/cli-surface/advisor-recommend.md              | 8 ++++----\n 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)\ndiff --git a/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog/cli-surface/advisor-recommend.md b/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog/cli-surface/advisor-recommend.md\nindex 22b508c123..378ffe88e4 100644\n--- a/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog/cli-surface/advisor-recommend.md\n+++ b/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog/cli-surface/advisor-recommend.md\n@@ -28,13 +28,13 @@ The caller-supplied `workspaceRoot` is bounded by `schemas/advisor-tool-schemas.\n \n ### Compiled-Routing Enrichment (`compiledRoute`)\n \n-Each recommendation carries an optional `compiledRoute` field (`schemas/advisor-tool-schemas.ts:308`, `z.record(z.string(), z.unknown()).optional()`). `handlers/advisor-recommend.ts`'s `enrichCompiledRoutes()` attaches it only when at least one recommended `skillId` is both in the fixed 7-hub `COMPILED_ROUTING_HUBS` set and currently permitted by the tri-state `SPECKIT_COMPILED_ROUTING` flag (`compiledRoutingEnabledForHub()`, from `../lib/compiled-routing-flag.ts`). Otherwise the schema re-parse is skipped entirely and the output returns unchanged. When enrichment runs, `compiledRouteForRecommendation()` shells out to `.skilled/bin/compiled-route.cjs --hub <skillId> --prompt-stdin`, writes the prompt to its stdin and attaches the parsed result. The one exception is a result whose `servingAuthority` is `\"legacy\"`: the field then stays absent, because a legacy sentinel is never surfaced as if it were a compiled decision. A subprocess failure is handled the same way: silently no `compiledRoute` field, with an optional debug-gated stderr breadcrumb via `SPECKIT_COMPILED_ROUTING_DEBUG`, so a probe failure degrades to exactly what an ineligible or flag-off recommendation already looks like. In short, `compiledRoute` is attached only for an eligible, flag-permitted hub that is genuinely serving compiled. It is intentionally absent for every other combination: flag off, hub not in `COMPILED_ROUTING_HUBS`, legacy sentinel or probe failure. See [`feature-flag-governance.md`](../../../system-spec-kit/feature-catalog/governance/feature-flag-governance.md) for the flag's phased-default and serving-status contract, and each eligible hub's own `compiled-routing-and-legacy-fallback.md` catalog leaf for the hub-side directive this enrichment mirrors. The front door runs from the request's `workspaceRoot`, and a caller may name another checkout there, such as a worktree under the repository root. So the handler first checks that the front door it would run reads `--prompt-stdin`. An older front door gets no call and the recommendation carries no `compiledRoute`, because it would route an empty prompt.\n+Each recommendation carries an optional `compiledRoute` field (the `compiledRoute` field of `AdvisorRecommendationSchema` in `schemas/advisor-tool-schemas.ts`, `z.record(z.string(), z.unknown()).optional()`). `handlers/advisor-recommend.ts`'s `enrichCompiledRoutes()` attaches it only when at least one recommended `skillId` is both in the fixed 7-hub `COMPILED_ROUTING_HUBS` set and currently permitted by the tri-state `SPECKIT_COMPILED_ROUTING` flag (`compiledRoutingEnabledForHub()`, from `../lib/compiled-routing-flag.ts`). Otherwise the schema re-parse is skipped entirely and the output returns unchanged. When enrichment runs, `compiledRouteForRecommendation()` shells out to `.skilled/bin/compiled-route.cjs --hub <skillId> --prompt-stdin`, writes the prompt to its stdin and attaches the parsed result. The one exception is a result whose `servingAuthority` is `\"legacy\"`: the field then stays absent, because a legacy sentinel is never surfaced as if it were a compiled decision. A subprocess failure is handled the same way: silently no `compiledRoute` field, with an optional debug-gated stderr breadcrumb via `SPECKIT_COMPILED_ROUTING_DEBUG`, so a probe failure degrades to exactly what an ineligible or flag-off recommendation already looks like. In short, `compiledRoute` is attached only for an eligible, flag-permitted hub that is genuinely serving compiled. It is intentionally absent for every other combination: flag off, hub not in `COMPILED_ROUTING_HUBS`, legacy sentinel or probe failure. See [`feature-flag-governance.md`](../../../system-spec-kit/feature-catalog/governance/feature-flag-governance.md) for the flag's phased-default and serving-status contract, and each eligible hub's own `compiled-routing-and-legacy-fallback.md` catalog leaf for the hub-side directive this enrichment mirrors. The front door runs from the request's `workspaceRoot`, and a caller may name another checkout there, such as a worktree under the repository root. So the handler first checks that the front door it would run reads `--prompt-stdin`. An older front door gets no call and the recommendation carries no `compiledRoute`, because it would route an empty prompt.\n \n-When a recommendation gets a `compiledRoute`, `enrichCompiledRoutes()` also asks `attachCommand()` in `lib/command-attach.ts` for a slash command and sets the optional `command` field when one comes back (`schemas/advisor-tool-schemas.ts:310`, `z.string().min(1).optional()`). `attachCommand()` names a command only for a `route` decision with `selectionKind: 'single'` and exactly one target, and only when the generated `MODE_COMMANDS` table maps that hub and `workflowMode` to a command. A bundle, a multi-target route or a mode with no command leaves `command` off. For `system-deep-loop` the prompt must type the same command or hold a phrase from `DEPTH_WORDING`, so a prompt that only names a topic such as research or review gets no deep-loop command. A prompt that matches `NO_EDIT_REQUEST` gets no command from any hub, because a reader who rules out a change is never handed work that writes.\n+When a recommendation gets a `compiledRoute`, `enrichCompiledRoutes()` also asks `attachCommand()` in `lib/command-attach.ts` for a slash command and sets the optional `command` field when one comes back (the `command` field of `AdvisorRecommendationSchema` in `schemas/advisor-tool-schemas.ts`, `z.string().min(1).optional()`). `attachCommand()` names a command only for a `route` decision with `selectionKind: 'single'` and exactly one target, and only when the generated `MODE_COMMANDS` table maps that hub and `workflowMode` to a command. A bundle, a multi-target route or a mode with no command leaves `command` off. For `system-deep-loop` the prompt must type the same command or hold a phrase from `DEPTH_WORDING`, so a prompt that only names a topic such as research or review gets no deep-loop command. A prompt that matches `NO_EDIT_REQUEST` gets no command from any hub, because a reader who rules out a change is never handed work that writes.\n \n-The request option `options.includeCompiledRoute` is an optional boolean that defaults to true. When a caller passes `false` the handler skips `enrichCompiledRoutes()` on both the fresh and the cached return (`handlers/advisor-recommend.ts:563-565`, `632-634`), so no `compiled-route.cjs` subprocess starts and no recommendation carries `compiledRoute` or `command`. The prompt hooks pass `true` (`hooks/lib/skill-advisor-cli-fallback.ts:238`), because the `command` field is derived from the compiled route. The OpenCode plugin does not pass the option and keeps receiving `compiledRoute`. The option is declared in the zod schema (`schemas/advisor-tool-schemas.ts:287`), the tool descriptor (`tools/advisor-recommend.ts:23`) and the CLI manifest (`skill-advisor-cli-manifest.ts:57`).\n+The request option `options.includeCompiledRoute` is an optional boolean that defaults to true. When a caller passes `false` the handler skips `enrichCompiledRoutes()` on both the fresh and the cached return (the two `input.options?.includeCompiledRoute === false` checks in `handlers/advisor-recommend.ts`), so no `compiled-route.cjs` subprocess starts and no recommendation carries `compiledRoute` or `command`. The prompt hooks pass `true` (`hooks/lib/skill-advisor-cli-fallback.ts:238`), because the `command` field is derived from the compiled route. The OpenCode plugin does not pass the option and keeps receiving `compiledRoute`. The option is declared in the zod schema (the `options` of `AdvisorRecommendInputSchema` in `schemas/advisor-tool-schemas.ts`), the tool descriptor (`tools/advisor-recommend.ts:23`) and the CLI manifest (`skill-advisor-cli-manifest.ts:57`).\n \n-The request option `options.compiledRouteTopOnly` is an optional boolean that defaults to false. When a caller passes `true`, `enrichCompiledRoutes()` runs the route lookup for the first recommendation only and returns every later one unchanged, so only the top pick can carry `compiledRoute` or `command`. Each lookup is a `compiled-route.cjs` subprocess, so this saves one subprocess for each further eligible hub. The prompt hooks pass `true` with `includeCompiledRoute: true`, because the brief leads with the top pick. The option is declared in the zod schema (`schemas/advisor-tool-schemas.ts:290`), the tool descriptor (`tools/advisor-recommend.ts:24`) and the CLI manifest (`skill-advisor-cli-manifest.ts:58`).\n+The request option `options.com